IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), Part III, ss 77-79: guardian's allowance and benefits for the aged. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
-- BAR POLARITY: a "shall not be entitled" function answers "is the person barred?": JUST TRUE = the text says not entitled;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no bar (a failed "if", an "unless" met, an exception); NOTHING = the rule is silent on the case.

§ `Part III -- Non-Contributory Benefits: guardian's allowance and benefits for the aged`

§§ `s 77 -- Guardian's allowance`

-- s 77(2): "The circumstances referred to in subsection (1)(b) above are" (a) both parents dead; (b) one parent dead and the claimant shows he was at the date of the death unaware of, and has failed after all reasonable efforts to discover, the whereabouts of the other;
-- (c) one parent dead and the other in prison. Subsection (8)(b) makes regulations prescribe when a person is treated as in prison, so (c) takes an input. Whether the circumstances are among these is what s 77(1)(b) asks ("any of those specified in subsection (2)").
-- src:2154 | (2) The circumstances referred to in subsection (1)(b) above are—
-- src:2155 | (a) that both of the parents of the child or qualifying young person are dead; or
-- src:2156 | (b) that one of the parents of the child or qualifying young person is dead and the person claiming a guardian’s allowance shows that he was at the date of the death unaware of, and has failed after all reasonable efforts to discover, the whereabouts of the other parent; or
-- src:2157 | (c) that one of the parents of the child or qualifying young person is dead and the other is in prison.
@ref s 77(2) (src:2154-2157)
GIVEN `both of the parents of the child or qualifying young person are dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the parents is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claiming shows that he was at the date of the death unaware of the whereabouts of the other parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person claiming has failed after all reasonable efforts to discover the whereabouts of the other parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other parent is in prison, treated as such under the regulations required by subsection (8)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(2) the circumstances are among those referred to in subsection (1)(b)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `both of the parents of the child or qualifying young person are dead` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (a)
        IF `one of the parents is dead` AND `the person claiming shows that he was at the date of the death unaware of the whereabouts of the other parent` AND `the person claiming has failed after all reasonable efforts to discover the whereabouts of the other parent` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (b)
        IF `one of the parents is dead` AND (`the other parent is in prison, treated as such under the regulations required by subsection (8)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE    -- (c)
        IF `one of the parents is dead` AND (`the other parent is in prison, treated as such under the regulations required by subsection (8)(b)` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (8)(b) leaves the meaning of "in prison" to regulations that are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the circumstances are any of those specified in subsection (2) below" and none of paragraphs (a) to (c) holds

-- s 77(1): "A person shall be entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person if" (a) he is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or young person, and (b) the circumstances are any of those specified in (2).
-- (Line 2153 is an editorial omission, "...", in this text.)
-- src:2150 | (1) A person shall be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person if—
-- src:2151 | (a) he is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person, and
-- src:2152 | (b) the circumstances are any of those specified in subsection (2) below.
@ref s 77(1) (src:2150-2152)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are among those referred to in subsection (1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(1) the person is entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of the child or qualifying young person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person if (a) he is entitled to child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person"
        IF `the circumstances are among those referred to in subsection (1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the circumstances are any of those specified in subsection (2) below"
        IF `the circumstances are among those referred to in subsection (1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the other parent is in prison turns on regulations that are not among the sources

-- s 77(3): "There shall be no entitlement to a guardian's allowance ... unless at least one of the parents satisfies, or immediately before his death satisfied, such conditions as may be prescribed as to nationality, residence, place of birth or other matters."
-- src:2158 | (3) There shall be no entitlement to a guardian’s allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person unless at least one of the parents of the child or qualifying young person satisfies, or immediately before his death satisfied, such conditions as may be prescribed as to nationality, residence, place of birth or other matters.
@ref s 77(3) (src:2158)
GIVEN `at least one of the parents satisfies, or immediately before his death satisfied, the prescribed conditions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(3) the person is barred from a guardian's allowance by the parents' conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `at least one of the parents satisfies, or immediately before his death satisfied, the prescribed conditions`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There shall be no entitlement ... unless at least one of the parents satisfies"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "There shall be no entitlement to a guardian's allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person unless"

-- s 77(5): "Those conditions are" (a) the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child living with him; or (b) the requisite contributions are being made to the cost of providing for the child.
-- (a) is Part IX's answer (s 143(1)(a) and (2), another part's range), an input; (b) is decided by subsection (6).
-- s 77(6): the condition in (5)(b) "is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if" (a) contributions are being made at a weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in (4) (i) by the beneficiary or (ii) where one of two spouses or civil partners residing together, by them together;
-- and (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying s 143(1)(b). The latter is seam S18 (Part IX's answer).
-- src:2163 | (6) The condition specified in subsection (5)(b) above is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if—
-- src:2164 | (a) such contributions are being made at a weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in subsection (4) above—
-- src:2165 | (i) by the beneficiary; or
-- src:2166 | (ii) where the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together, by them together; and
-- src:2167 | (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above those required for the purpose of satisfying section 143(1)(b) below.
@ref s 77(6) (src:2163-2167)
GIVEN `the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly rate at which the beneficiary is making contributions in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate at which the two spouses or civil partners together are making contributions in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the case is a prescribed case` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(6) the condition in subsection (5)(b) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `paragraph (a)` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be treated as satisfied if, but only if ... (a) such contributions are being made at a weekly rate not less than the amount referred to in subsection (4) above"
        IF `the case is a prescribed case` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE    -- "except in prescribed cases" paragraph (b) is not required
        IF `s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 143(1)(b) the contributions are over and above those required for satisfying section 143(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the case is a prescribed case` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, but only if ... (b) except in prescribed cases, the contributions are over and above those required for the purpose of satisfying section 143(1)(b) below"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 143(1)(b), or the prescribed cases, are not among the sources
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
               (`the weekly rate at which the beneficiary is making contributions in pounds` AT LEAST `the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable in pounds`)
            OR (`the beneficiary is one of two spouses or civil partners residing together`
                AND (`the weekly rate at which the two spouses or civil partners together are making contributions in pounds` AT LEAST `the weekly amount of guardian's allowance otherwise payable in pounds`))

-- s 77(4): "Where, apart from this subsection, a person is entitled to receive ... payment of an amount by way of a guardian's allowance, that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (5) below is satisfied."
-- src:2159 | (4) Where, apart from this subsection, a person is entitled to receive, in respect of a particular child or qualifying young person, payment of an amount by way of a guardian’s allowance, that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (5) below is satisfied.
-- src:2160 | (5) Those conditions are—
-- src:2161 | (a) that the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX of this Act as having the child or qualifying young person living with him; or
-- src:2162 | (b) that the requisite contributions are being made to the cost of providing for the child or qualifying young person.
@ref s 77(4) (src:2159-2162)
GIVEN `s 143 the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the condition in subsection (5)(b) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(4) the amount is barred from payment by the conditions in subsection (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 143 the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the condition in subsection (5)(b) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (5) below is satisfied"
        IF (`s 143 the beneficiary would be treated for the purposes of Part IX as having the child or qualifying young person living with him` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the condition in subsection (5)(b) is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative with "unless" not met): "that amount shall not be payable unless one of the conditions specified in subsection (5) below is satisfied"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Part IX's answer, or section 143(1)(b), is not supplied

-- s 77(7): "A guardian's allowance ... shall be payable at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 5." The table is omitted from this text, so the rate is an input.
-- src:2168 | (7) A guardian’s allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person shall be payable at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 5.
@ref s 77(7) (src:2168)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt III para 5 the weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77(7) the weekly rate of a guardian's allowance in pounds` MEANS
    `sch 4 pt III para 5 the weekly rate of guardian's allowance in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied

-- s 77(8) (regulations may modify (2) and (3) for adopted or illegitimate children; shall prescribe when a person is in prison; may require repayment, suspend payment and reduce the rate) is a set of regulation-making powers (inert, machinery).

-- s 77(9): "Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of the same child ..., only the woman shall be entitled".
-- src:2176 | (9) Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person, only the woman shall be entitled, but payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him.
@ref s 77(9) (src:2176)
GIVEN sex IS A Sex
      `a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `apart from this subsection they would each be entitled in respect of the same child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(9) the person is the one who is entitled to the guardian's allowance` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together` AND `apart from this subsection they would each be entitled in respect of the same child or qualifying young person`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for "a man and woman" who are married or civil partners, residing together, each entitled apart from the subsection
    ELSE CONSIDER sex
         WHEN Woman THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Man THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only the woman shall be entitled"

-- s 77(9), payment: "payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him."
-- src:2176 | (9) Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person, only the woman shall be entitled, but payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him.
@ref s 77(9) (src:2176)
GIVEN `a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(9) payment may be made to the man` MEANS
    IF   NOT (`a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together`)
    THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for "a man and woman" who are married or civil partners and residing together
    ELSE IF `the woman elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him`
         THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 77(9) as a regulative rule: the woman MAY elect, in the prescribed manner. The text states no time limit and no consequence beyond the election itself, and none is invented.
-- src:2176 | (9) Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person, only the woman shall be entitled, but payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him.
@ref s 77(9) (src:2176)
DECLARE `s 77(9) Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 77(9) the woman`

-- src:2176 | (9) Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person, only the woman shall be entitled, but payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him.
@ref s 77(9) (src:2176)
DECLARE `s 77(9) Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 77(9) elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to the man`

-- src:2176 | (9) Where a man and woman are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, and, apart from this subsection, they would each be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of the same child or qualifying young person, only the woman shall be entitled, but payment may be made either to her or to him unless she elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to him.
@ref s 77(9) (src:2176)
`s 77(9) the woman may elect that payment is not to be made to the man` MEANS
    PARTY `s 77(9) the woman`
    MAY `s 77(9) elects in the prescribed manner that payment is not to be made to the man`

-- s 77(11): "Where a person (a) has adopted a child or qualifying young person; and (b) was entitled to guardian's allowance in respect of the child ... immediately before the adoption, subsection (10) shall not terminate his entitlement."
-- src:2178 | (11) Where a person—
-- src:2179 | (a) has adopted a child or qualifying young person ; and
-- src:2180 | (b) was entitled to guardian’s allowance in respect of the child or qualifying young person immediately before the adoption,
-- src:2181 | subsection (10) above shall not terminate his entitlement.
@ref s 77(11) (src:2178-2181)
GIVEN `the person has adopted the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was entitled to guardian's allowance in respect of the child or qualifying young person immediately before the adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(11) subsection (10) does not terminate the person's entitlement` MEANS
    IF   `the person has adopted the child or qualifying young person` AND `the person was entitled to guardian's allowance in respect of the child or qualifying young person immediately before the adoption`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no to the termination (a flat negative): "subsection (10) above shall not terminate his entitlement"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for a person who has adopted the child and was entitled immediately before the adoption

-- s 77(10): "Subject to subsection (11) below, no person shall be entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person of which he or she is the parent."
-- src:2177 | (10) Subject to subsection (11) below, no person shall be entitled to a guardian’s allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person of which he or she is the parent.
@ref s 77(10) (src:2177)
GIVEN `the person is the parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (11) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 77(10) the person is barred from a guardian's allowance because he or she is the parent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the parent of the child or qualifying young person`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for a child "of which he or she is the parent"
        IF `subsection (11) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (11) below" and "subsection (10) above shall not terminate his entitlement"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "no person shall be entitled to a guardian's allowance in respect of a child or qualifying young person of which he or she is the parent"

§§ `s 78 -- Category C and Category D retirement pensions and other benefits for the aged`

-- s 78(4): the elements to disregard when comparing the rate of a Category A, B or C pension with the appropriate weekly rate: (a) any additional pension; (b) any increase attributable to (i) additional pension or (ii) an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension; (c) any graduated retirement benefit; (d) blank in this text.
-- src:2189 | (4) The elements referred to in subsection (3)(b) above are—
-- src:2190 | (a) any additional pension;
-- src:2191 | (b) any increase so far as attributable to—
-- src:2192 | (i) any additional pension, or
-- src:2193 | (ii) any increase in a guaranteed minimum pension;
-- src:2194 | (c) any graduated retirement benefit; and
-- src:2195 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 78(4) (src:2189-2195)
GIVEN `the weekly rate at which the pension is payable in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `any additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `any increase attributable to additional pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `any increase attributable to an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `any graduated retirement benefit in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 78(4) the weekly rate of the pension disregarding the elements in pounds` MEANS
    `the weekly rate at which the pension is payable in pounds`
        MINUS `any additional pension in pounds`
        MINUS `any increase attributable to additional pension in pounds`
        MINUS `any increase attributable to an increase in a guaranteed minimum pension in pounds`
        MINUS `any graduated retirement benefit in pounds`

-- s 78(3): "A person who is over the age of 80, who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and who satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed shall be entitled to a Category D retirement pension at the appropriate weekly rate if"
-- (a) he is not entitled to a Category A, B or C retirement pension; or (b) he is entitled to such a pension, but it is payable at a weekly rate which, disregarding the elements in (4), is less than the appropriate weekly rate.
-- A person outside the class (not over 80, or reaching pensionable age on or after 6 April 2016, or not meeting the prescribed conditions) is outside the sentence: NOTHING. Within the class the "if" decides.
-- src:2186 | (3) A person who is over the age of 80 , who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and who satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed shall be entitled to a Category D retirement pension at the appropriate weekly rate if—
-- src:2187 | (a) he is not entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category C retirement pension; or
-- src:2188 | (b) he is entitled to such a pension, but it is payable at a weekly rate which, disregarding those elements specified in subsection (4) below, is less than the appropriate weekly rate.
@ref s 78(3) (src:2186-2188)
GIVEN person IS A Person
      `s 173(a) the person is over 80` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category C retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the weekly rate of that pension disregarding the elements in subsection (4) in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `sch 4 pt III para 7 the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(3) the person is entitled to a Category D retirement pension` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (person's `date of attaining pensionable age` LESS THAN (Date 6 4 2016)) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016"
        IF (`s 173(a) the person is over 80` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the person satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "A person who is over the age of 80 ... and who satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed"
        IF (`s 173(a) the person is over 80` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the person satisfies such conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the age answer, or the prescribed conditions, are not supplied
        IF NOT `the person is entitled to a Category A, Category B or Category C retirement pension` THEN JUST TRUE    -- (a)
        IF `the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension is known` AND (`the weekly rate of that pension disregarding the elements in subsection (4) in pounds` LESS THAN `the appropriate weekly rate`) THEN JUST TRUE    -- (b)
        IF `the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension is known` AND NOT (`the weekly rate of that pension disregarding the elements in subsection (4) in pounds` LESS THAN `the appropriate weekly rate`) THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be entitled to a Category D retirement pension at the appropriate weekly rate if ... (b) he is entitled to such a pension, but it is payable at a weekly rate which, disregarding those elements specified in subsection (4) below, is less than the appropriate weekly rate"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the appropriate weekly rate is in Schedule 4, whose table is omitted from this text
    WHERE
        `the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension is known` MEANS NOT (`sch 4 pt III para 7 the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` EQUALS NOTHING)
        `the appropriate weekly rate` MEANS
            CONSIDER `sch 4 pt III para 7 the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds`
            WHEN JUST rate THEN rate
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- s 78(6): "The appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension shall be that specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 7." The table is omitted from this text.
-- src:2197 | (6) The appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension shall be that specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 7.
@ref s 78(6) (src:2197)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt III para 7 the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 78(6) the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds` MEANS
    `sch 4 pt III para 7 the appropriate weekly rate of a Category D retirement pension in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied

-- s 78(7): "Entitlement to a ... Category D retirement pension shall continue throughout the pensioner's life."
-- src:2198 | (7) Entitlement to a ... Category D retirement pension shall continue throughout the pensioner’s life.
@ref s 78(7) (src:2198)
GIVEN `the pensioner is entitled to a Category D retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pensioner is alive on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(7) the entitlement continues on the day` MEANS
    IF   `the pensioner is entitled to a Category D retirement pension` AND `the pensioner is alive on the day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall continue throughout the pensioner's life" says nothing of a day after the pensioner's life or of a person not yet entitled

-- s 78(8): "A ... Category D retirement pension shall not be payable for any period falling before the day on which the pensioner's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing ... by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act."
-- src:2199 | (8) A ... Category D retirement pension shall not be payable for any period falling before the day on which the pensioner’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act.
@ref s 78(8) (src:2199)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which the entitlement is to be regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78(8) the Category D retirement pension is barred from payment for the day` MEANS
    IF   day LESS THAN `the day on which the entitlement is to be regarded as commencing under section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE    -- the text says no (a flat negative): "shall not be payable for any period falling before the day on which the pensioner's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing"
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar covers "any period falling before" the commencing day

-- s 78(1), (2), (4)(d) and (5) are shown blank in this text. s 78(9) (regulations may provide for Category C pensions at the prescribed rate) is a regulation-making power (inert, machinery).

§§ `s 79 -- Age addition`

-- s 79(1): "A person who is over the age of 80 and entitled to a retirement pension of any category under this Act shall be entitled to an increase of the pension, to be known as “age addition”."
-- src:2205 | (1) A person who is over the age of 80 and entitled to a retirement pension of any category under this Act shall be entitled to an increase of the pension, to be known as “age addition”.
@ref s 79(1) (src:2205)
GIVEN `s 173(a) the person is over 80` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to a retirement pension of a category under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) the person is entitled to an age addition to a retirement pension` MEANS
    IF   (`s 173(a) the person is over 80` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is entitled to a retirement pension of a category under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence grants to "A person who is over the age of 80 and entitled to a retirement pension" and does not say a person outside it is not entitled

-- s 79(2): "Where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of any prescribed enactment or instrument ... and (a) he is over the age of 80; and (b) he fulfils such other conditions as may be prescribed, he shall be entitled to an increase".
-- src:2206 | (2) Where a person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of any prescribed enactment or instrument (whether passed or made before or after this Act) and—
-- src:2207 | (a) he is over the age of 80; and
-- src:2208 | (b) he fulfils such other conditions as may be prescribed,
-- src:2209 | he shall be entitled to an increase of that pension or allowance, also known as age addition.
@ref s 79(2) (src:2206-2209)
GIVEN `the person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the person is over 80` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person fulfils such other conditions as may be prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2) the person is entitled to an age addition to another pension or allowance` MEANS
    IF   (`the person is in receipt of a pension or allowance payable by the Secretary of State by virtue of a prescribed enactment or instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`s 173(a) the person is over 80` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`the person fulfils such other conditions as may be prescribed` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the enactments and the conditions are prescribed by regulations that are not among the sources; the sentence grants and does not say a person outside it is not entitled

-- s 79(3): "Age addition shall be payable for the life of the person entitled, at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 8."
-- src:2210 | (3) Age addition shall be payable for the life of the person entitled, at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 8.
@ref s 79(3) (src:2210)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to an age addition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is alive on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(3) the age addition is payable on the day` MEANS
    IF   `the person is entitled to an age addition` AND `the person is alive on the day`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable for the life of the person entitled" says nothing of a day after the person's life

-- src:2210 | (3) Age addition shall be payable for the life of the person entitled, at the weekly rate specified in Schedule 4, Part III, paragraph 8.
@ref s 79(3) (src:2210)
GIVEN `sch 4 pt III para 8 the weekly rate of age addition in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 79(3) the weekly rate of age addition in pounds` MEANS
    `sch 4 pt III para 8 the weekly rate of age addition in pounds`    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) if the Schedule 4 figure is not supplied
